<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Round Table Talks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as National Round Table</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian Round Table Talks were negotiations held from June to September 1989 between the ruling communist party and the opposition. They agreed on free multi-party elections, a constitutional court and a presidency, amending the constitution so that the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was proclaimed on 23 October 1989. The first free elections followed in spring 1990.</p></div>
